  "verbalization": "Usararotenoid C appears to be a target for multiple compounds that are ultimately linked to Carboxylesterase 2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Usararotenoid C acts as a target for SNU-387, a compound that is itself a target of other molecules, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol. These compounds all share a common pathway leading to Carboxylesterase 2, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving enzyme inhibition or modulation. The integration of these pathways suggests that Usararotenoid C may interact with these compounds, which in turn inhibit Carboxylesterase 2, potentially through a shared mechanism of action. The evidence supports a relationship where Usararotenoid C is indirectly linked to Carboxylesterase 2 via these molecular intermediates, highlighting a possible role in enzyme inhibition or regulation.",
